{
  "requirement": "Listing and reading failures return errors, distinct from successful empty\nlistings and successful reads of empty files.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately cover `requirements.sdk.sources.provider.errors`. The requirement has three testable parts: listing failures return errors, reading failures return errors, and both stay distinct from successful empty results.\n\n**Listing failures**\n- `failed_provider_operations_never_become_successful_empty_results` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs` uses `FailingProvider`. It runs with `list_fails` set to true and false.\n- It asserts that `search_text` returns an error with the message \"listing failed\" when listing fails.\n- It asserts the same for `search_structure` when the `default-languages` feature is enabled.\n- In `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs`, `empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct` shows `Sources::list` returning an error. The cases are a root that is a file, a root that does not exist, and a missing prefix scope.\n- `scoped_inspection_skips_unrelated_directories_and_reports_relevant_ignore_errors` shows listing errors from a broken `.gitignore` and from a symlink in scope.\n\n**Reading failures**\n- `FailingProvider::read` always errors. The first test asserts \"reading failed\" for `search_text`, `parse` and `search_structure`.\n- On the filesystem provider, reads of missing files, `../` paths and absolute paths return errors. The ignore-error read of `broken/target.txt` does too.\n\n**Distinct from successful empty results**\n- `successful_empty_listing_and_empty_resources_are_distinct_from_errors` uses `Primitives`. It asserts that an empty listing returns `Ok` with length 0, and that an empty file returns `Ok` with empty bytes.\n- The same test asserts that `parse`, `search_text` and `search_structure` over empty inputs return `Ok` with `complete` true and no matches.\n- `empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct` shows the real `Sources` returning an empty `Ok` listing for an empty directory and an empty `Ok` read for an empty file, next to the error cases above.\n- `completeness_is_false_only_when_a_match_is_omitted_and_errors_propagate` also covers errors propagating, with an invalid pattern and with invalid UTF-8 or an unknown language in `parse_snapshot`.\n\nEvery obligation (list errors, read errors, empty-listing success, empty-read success) has a test that exercises it and asserts the outcome. All the tests carry `{test}` references to the requirement. I found no gaps.",
  "references": "4b9203b0a488dc4487cc9c5b785258007920be5ad703e2cd52ebadf5d9e380bc",
